d across  the board with the lg c2 we'll be also  getting a brand new gaming manual  users will be able to see the concurrent  refresh rates as well and ensure that  you're getting maximum frames in terms  of picture modes i've kept it to  standard as i feel it's optimal for my  use but feel free to play around with  these settings to ensure that it's  perfect for your own use while the  display does allow for ultra wide modes  in the form of a 32x9 and 21x9  these modes look weird and does come off  a bit pixelated hence my preferred  option is to keep it to windowed mode  for certain games and it allows me to  multitask as well when streaming  after having cycled through android tv  samsung's tizen os  lg's web os is okay by most standards  my preference is towards the v-mode  style remote controller  it's great as it allows you to navigate  around manuals pretty quickly  it's not the worst ui out there but it  does feel slightly slower than last  year's c1 model navigating between menus  doesn't feel that snappy compared to  other brands and it's something lg would  need to take note of as they work  towards their next iteration  order wise this is an area that  potential buyers of the 42-inch lg c2  need to take note off  because of its overall smaller footprint  the tv has 20 watt speakers instead of  40 watt speakers found in its 48 inch c2  models and larger this results in lower  sound volumes overall but it should not  matter if you're using headphones with  this tv  the tricky point in this juncture is  really down to price  across all the prices we have seen the  42-inch lg c2 tv is pretty close in  price point to the 48-inch model while  the size does justify the practical use  the difference in price might not  as much as we like to recommend the  42-inch lg c2 right off the bat it might  be an even more prudent choice to pick  this up when it goes on sale knowing lg  these discounts come pretty hard and  fast  when it comes to practical use the 42  inch lg c2 is definitely right size to  be used as a computer monitor for  everyday use if you are looking for a  16x9 display  if curved gaming monitors are more of  your thing  the alienware is the strong alternative  do check out the rest of the videos on  gaming displays right here  from a hardware standpoint the rog  pg48uq is a solid contender if you are  looking for a oled display alternatives  outside of lg especially for pc use
 

